{"t": 1794106966.3242574, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_reply_to_pull_request_comment", "args": {"body": "Done \u2014 the parameter is now `amount_cents`, so the unit is in the name:\n\n```python\ndef make_entry(account: str, amount_cents: int) -> dict:\n    ...\n    return {\"account\": account, \"amount_cents\": amount_cents}\n```\n\nCallers passing it by keyword will need the new name; there are no other call sites in this repo.", "commentId": 90011, "owner": "acme", "pullNumber": 88, "repo": "ledger"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794106967.3325698, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_reply_to_pull_request_comment", "args": {"body": "Added the guard in `ledger/entries.py`:\n\n```python\nif amount_cents < 0:\n    raise ValueError(f\"amount_cents must be non-negative, got {amount_cents}\")\n```\n\nZero is still allowed (only negatives are rejected), and no refund logic was added here since refunds use their own entry type.", "commentId": 90012, "owner": "acme", "pullNumber": 88, "repo": "ledger"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794106969.4526584, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_or_update_file", "args": {"branch": "entry-helper", "content": "def make_entry(account: str, amount_cents: int) -> dict:\n    if amount_cents < 0:\n        raise ValueError(f\"amount_cents must be non-negative, got {amount_cents}\")\n    return {\"account\": account, \"amount_cents\": amount_cents}\n", "message": "Rename amt to amount_cents and reject negative amounts", "owner": "acme", "path": "ledger/entries.py", "repo": "ledger"}, "ok": true}
